42 17592186045417 true] [17592186445182 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445182 1071 "The values of functions $q(x)$ and $z(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=7$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $q(x)$ | $z(x)$ | ${q}^{′}(x)$ | ${z}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $7$ | $-4$ | $-6$ | $8$ | $10$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4q(x)-3z(x))$ at $x=7.$" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445182 1072 #uuid "185be666-6314-550d-b382-232010c7dadf" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445182 1074 "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4q(x)-3z(x))=4{q}^{′}(x)-3{z}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=7$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4q(x)-3z(x))|}_{x=7} & =4{q}^{′}(7)-3{z}^{′}(7) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 8-3\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =32-30 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445183 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445176 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445183 1069 "q-341022" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445183 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445183 1071 "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x),$ you are given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(-1)=\\sqrt{3},\\,{f}^{′}(-1)=\\sqrt{3},\\,g(-1)=-3,\\,{g}^{′}(-1)=2\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})$ at $x=-1.$ Do not round the answer. \n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=-1}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445183 1072 #uuid "2c1d20bb-7423-5d1e-aef5-963d443861a9" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445183 1074 "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-1,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=-1} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(-1)g(-1)-f(-1){g}^{′}(-1)}{(g(-1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\cdot (-3)-\\sqrt{3}\\cdot (2)}{(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3\\sqrt{3}-2\\sqrt{3}}{9} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445184 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445174 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445184 1069 "q-341455" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445184 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445184 1071 "For the functions $p(x)$ and $q(x),$ you're given the following data:\n\n$$\np(5)=-2,\\,{p}^{′}(5)=3,\\,q(5)=1,\\,{q}^{′}(5)=-4\n$$\n\nIf $z(x)=(p(x)+2q(x))(3-p(x)),$ compute ${z}^{′}(5).$\n\n${z}^{′}(5)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445184 1072 #uuid "33fa495c-c75d-54c3-993a-6917944aba8b" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445184 1074 "The product rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(uv)=u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=p(x)+2q(x)$ and $v=3-p(x).$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={p}^{′}(x)+2{q}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=-{p}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}(x) & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =(p(x)+2q(x))(-{p}^{′}(x))+(3-p(x))({p}^{′}(x)+2{q}^{′}(x)) \\\\  & =-{p}^{′}(x)(p(x)+2q(x))+(3-p(x))({p}^{′}(x)+2{q}^{′}(x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=5$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}(5) & =-{p}^{′}(5)(p(5)+2q(5))+(3-p(5))({p}^{′}(5)+2{q}^{′}(5)) \\\\  & =-(3)(-2+2\\cdot 1)+(3-(-2))(3+2\\cdot (-4)) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot 0+5\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445185 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445179 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445185 1069 "q-340986" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445185 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445185 1071 "For the function $f(x)$ and $g(x)$, you're given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(-2)=-3,\\,{f}^{′}(-2)=\\frac{1}{2},\\,g(-2)=4,\\,{g}^{′}(-2)=-2\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))$ at $x=-2.$\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=-2}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445185 1072 #uuid "5bb65209-2ef4-5e75-8f8a-170aaa43e597" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445185 1074 "Using the product rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x)) & =f(x){g}^{′}(x)+g(x){f}^{′}(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-2$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=-2} & =f(-2){g}^{′}(-2)+g(-2){f}^{′}(-2) \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot (-2)+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445186 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445175 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445186 1069 "q-311283" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445186 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445186 1071 "The values of functions $h(x)$ and $z(x)$ and their derivatives at $t=3$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $h(t)$ | $z(t)$ | ${h}^{′}(t)$ | ${z}^{′}(t)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $-2$ | $6$ | $5$ | $-1$ |\n\nIf $f(t)=\\frac{2+h(t)}{z(t)},$ compute  ${f}^{′}(3).$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}^{′}(3)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445186 1072 #uuid "820989f9-6d7d-594e-a9c9-c00397b747b4" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445186 1074 "The quotient rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{u}{v})=\\frac{{u}^{′}v-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=2+h(t)$ and $v=z(t).$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}={h}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}={z}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the quotient rule gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(t)=\\frac{{h}^{′}(t)z(t)-(2+h(t)){z}^{′}(t)}{{z}^{2}(t)}.\n$$\n\nAt $t=3,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(3) & =\\frac{{h}^{′}(3)z(3)-(2+h(3)){z}^{′}(3)}{{z}^{2}(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 6-(2+(-2))(-1)}{{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{30-(0)(-1)}{36} \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{36} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445187 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445177 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445187 1069 "q-311275" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445187 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445187 1071 "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=2$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $4$ | $-3$ | $2$ | $5$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))$ at $x=2.$\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=2}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445187 1072 #uuid "c4c74154-74a4-59d0-b3a0-d5c61e076d93" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445187 1074 "Using the product rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))=f(x){g}^{′}(x)+g(x){f}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=2$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=2} & =f(2){g}^{′}(2)+g(2){f}^{′}(2) \\\\  & =(4)(5)+(-3)(2) \\\\  & =20-6 \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445188 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445173 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445188 1069 "q-72991" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445188 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445188 1071 "The values of functions $q(x)$ and $r(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=4$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $q(x)$ | $r(x)$ | ${q}^{′}(x)$ | ${r}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $-5$ | $3$ | $4$ | $-7$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2q(x)+3r(x))$ at $x=4.$" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445188 1072 #uuid "c69fac4d-ae7b-5cea-a5ac-be4dd3c238bf" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445188 1074 "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2q(x)+3r(x))=2{q}^{′}(x)+3{r}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=4$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2q(x)+3r(x))|}_{x=4} & =2{q}^{′}(4)+3{r}^{′}(4) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 4+3\\cdot (-7) \\\\  & =8-21 \\\\  & =-13.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445189 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445180 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445189 1069 "q-341023" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445189 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445189 1071 "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x),$ you are given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(0)=3,\\,{f}^{′}(0)=2,\\,g(0)=\\frac{1}{2},\\,{g}^{′}(0)=-1\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})$ at $x=0.$\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=0}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445189 1072 #uuid "d746f1cc-0701-523c-a4d0-da44e37048c9" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445189 1074 "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=0,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=0} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(0)g(0)-f(0){g}^{′}(0)}{(g(0))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2})-3\\cdot (-1)}{{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+3}{\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445190 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445178 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445190 1069 "q-340450" 13194139534942 17592186045417 true] [17592186445190 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534942 17592186